DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     These functions provide text descriptions of _s_t_r_u_c_t _k_e_v_e_n_t fields.

     The ssyyssddeeccooddee__kkeevveenntt__ffffllaaggss() function outputs a text description of the
     _f_f_l_a_g_s member of a _s_t_r_u_c_t _k_e_v_e_n_t to the stream _f_p.  For the EVFILT_READ,
     EVFILT_WRITE, EVFILT_VNODE, EVFILT_PROC, EVFILT_PROCDESC, EVFILT_TIMER,
     and EVFILT_USER filters, ssyyssddeeccooddee__kkeevveenntt__ffffllaaggss() outputs a bitmask of
     filter-specific NOTE_* flags as documented in kevent(2).  For other val‐
     ues of _f_i_l_t_e_r, the value of _f_f_l_a_g_s is output in the indicated _b_a_s_e (one
     of 8, 10, or 16).

     The ssyyssddeeccooddee__kkeevveenntt__ffiilltteerr() function returns a text description of the
     _f_i_l_t_e_r member of a _s_t_r_u_c_t _k_e_v_e_n_t.  NULL is returned if the _f_i_l_t_e_r value
     is unknown.

     The ssyyssddeeccooddee__kkeevveenntt__ffllaaggss() function outputs a text description of the
     _f_l_a_g_s member of a _s_t_r_u_c_t _k_e_v_e_n_t to the stream _f_p.  This function uses the
     same calling convention and formatting as the other functions described
     in sysdecode_mask(3).

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     The ssyyssddeeccooddee__kkeevveenntt__ffiilltteerr function returns the name of a filter or NULL
     if the filter value is unknown.

     The ssyyssddeeccooddee__kkeevveenntt__ffllaaggss function returns true if any flags in the
     _f_l_a_g_s field were decoded and false if no flags were decoded.

